# Firebase localhost credentials

Firebase is **auth only** (project **`careflow-kenya`**). Product data is PostgreSQL. Do **not** create another Firebase project unless the user cannot access this one and asks.

Canonical walkthrough: **[ONBOARDING.md](../../ONBOARDING.md#firebase-localhost)**.

## When to prompt

Run the walkthrough (do not wait to be asked) when **any** of these are true:

- First-time setup, clone, onboarding, or “run the app”
- `docker compose`, `npm run dev`, or `GET /me`
- 401 `unauthorized`, log line `Firebase Admin credentials are not configured`, or empty `FIREBASE_*` in Compose
- `phantom_list_secrets` (names only) is missing `FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID`, `FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL`, or `FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY`

`GET /health` succeeding does **not** mean Firebase is configured.

## How to guide

1. Never ask the user to paste the service-account JSON, `private_key`, or ID tokens into chat.
2. Prefer Phantom MCP `phantom_add_secret_interactive` / `phantom_list_secrets`. Fallback: `phantom add VAR_NAME` in the terminal (value entry stays in the prompt).
3. Human generates the key at [Service accounts](https://console.firebase.google.com/project/careflow-kenya/settings/serviceaccounts/adminsdk). Map JSON → `FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID` (`careflow-kenya`), `FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL`, `FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY`.
4. Restart API with `phantom exec -- docker compose up --build -d`. PWA client keys are already in `frontend/lib/firebase-config.ts` (not Admin secrets).
5. Demo logins: [ONBOARDING.md](../../ONBOARDING.md#local-demo-accounts). The web `apiKey` is not `FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY`.
